2026-08-06T22:33:39.3494224Z Description:
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3494534Z     The `rails new` command creates a new Rails application with a default
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3495072Z     directory structure and configuration at the path you specify.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3495358Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3495542Z     You can specify extra command-line arguments to be used every time
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3496000Z     `rails new` runs in the .railsrc configuration file in your home directory,
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3496430Z     or in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rails/railsrc if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3496666Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3496861Z     Note that the arguments specified in the .railsrc file don't affect the
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3497258Z     default values shown above in this help message.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3497461Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3497666Z     You can specify which version to use when creating a new rails application 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498039Z     using `rails _<version>_ new`.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498205Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498279Z Examples:
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498473Z     `rails new ~/Code/Ruby/weblog`
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498644Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3498782Z     This generates a new Rails app in ~/Code/Ruby/weblog.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499004Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499098Z     `rails _<version>_ new weblog`
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499256Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499436Z     This generates a new Rails app with the provided version in ./weblog.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499708Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499802Z     `rails new weblog --api`
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3499960Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3500097Z     This generates a new Rails app in API mode in ./weblog.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3500344Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3500455Z     `rails new weblog --skip-action-mailer`
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3500646Z 
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3500812Z     This generates a new Rails app without Action Mailer in ./weblog.
2026-08-06T22:33:39.3501223Z     Any part of Rails can be skipped during app generation.
